  "note": "Settles back onto its haunches, holds, and rises again, so it loops as one clip in the bench. A game would cut it into sit-down / sit-idle / stand-up at the hold, which is why the hold is a flat pair of identical keys rather than a single instant. A two-legged sitter has no forelegs to prop on, so the tail takes the weight: it swings out behind and flattens as the body comes down.",
